# AirSense — Project Goal

## 1. Project Goal

Build a real-time interactive 3D IT office environment that visualizes how **occupancy, ventilation, Chennai outdoor weather, outdoor air quality, and indoor environmental conditions** change over time.

The application will initially work completely without physical sensors by using **dummy/simulated real-time data**.

Physical sensors will be integrated later without changing the core application architecture.

---

## 2. Main Objective

The application should make indoor environmental conditions easy to understand visually.

Instead of displaying only numbers:

    CO₂: 1200 ppm
    Temperature: 26°C
    Humidity: 60%

the application should show:

    People increase
          ↓
    Occupancy changes
          ↓
    Indoor environment changes
          ↓
    CO₂ / Temperature / Humidity change
          ↓
    Airflow visualization changes
          ↓
    Environmental status changes
          ↓
    Alert / Recommendation

---

## 3. Chennai Weather Integration

Use a weather API to retrieve current Chennai outdoor conditions.

The application should display:

- Outdoor temperature
- Outdoor humidity
- Wind speed
- Wind direction
- Weather condition
- Rain information where available
- Outdoor AQI where a reliable API is available

Outdoor data should be clearly separated from indoor data.

    OUTDOOR
       ↓
    Chennai Weather / AQI
       ↓
    Indoor Environment Simulation

Outdoor weather must NOT be treated as direct indoor measurements.

---

## 4. Adjustable Office Environment

Everything important in the office should be configurable.

### Room

- Width
- Length
- Height
- Capacity

### People

- Number of people
- Add person
- Remove person
- People distribution
- People per zone

### Ventilation

- Ventilation level
- Fresh-air input
- Airflow

### AC

- AC level
- Cooling effect

### Doors / Windows

- Open
- Closed

---

## 5. Indoor Environmental Parameters

The application should visualize:

- CO₂
- O₂
- Temperature
- Humidity
- Ventilation
- Airflow
- Occupancy
- Environmental status

Values generated by simulation must be clearly identified as simulated.

Example:

    CO₂: 920 ppm
    Source: Simulation

---

## 6. Real-Time Mode

The application must have a real-time simulation mode.

Example:

    Time: 10:30:25

    People:       45
    CO₂:          920 ppm
    O₂:           20.8 %
    Temperature:  24.8 °C
    Humidity:     57 %
    Ventilation:  70 %
    Airflow:      Normal
    Status:       🟡 Attention

Values should update automatically without refreshing the page.

---

## 7. Simulation Engine

Create a centralized environment simulation engine.

    Occupancy
         +
    Room Size
         +
    Ventilation
         +
    AC
         +
    Outdoor Conditions
         ↓
    Environment Simulation
         ↓
    CO₂ / Temperature / Humidity
         ↓
    Status Engine
         ↓
    3D Office + Dashboard

Do not generate unrelated random values independently in different UI components.

All components must receive their data from the same simulation state.

---

## 8. Occupancy Simulation

The user should be able to increase and decrease the number of people.

Example:

    20 → 40 → 60 → 80 people

The office should visually update as people enter or leave.

The environmental simulation should respond to occupancy changes.

---

## 9. Environmental Status

Use three visual states:

### Green

Normal environmental condition.

### Yellow

Environmental condition requires attention.

### Red

Environmental condition requires investigation/action.

The colors represent **environmental status**, not medical diagnosis.

---

## 10. Airflow Visualization

Display airflow using animated particles or arrows.

Example:

    → → → → → → →
    → → → → → → →
    → → → → → → →

Increasing ventilation should increase the visual airflow.

The airflow visualization is illustrative and is not intended to be a CFD simulation.

---

## 11. Dashboard

The dashboard should contain:

- Occupancy card
- CO₂ card
- O₂ card
- Temperature card
- Humidity card
- Ventilation card
- Airflow indicator
- Environmental status

Also provide:

- Live charts
- Historical charts
- Alerts
- Recommendations

---

## 12. Scenario Mode

Provide predefined scenarios.

### Normal Office

    Normal occupancy
    Normal ventilation
    Green status

### Increasing Occupancy

    People ↑
    CO₂ trend ↑
    Environmental condition changes

### Poor Ventilation

    People = high
    Ventilation = low
    CO₂ trend increases

### Improved Ventilation

    Ventilation ↑
    CO₂ trend ↓
    Environmental status improves

### Reduced Occupancy

    People ↓
    Environmental load ↓

---

## 13. Data Provider Architecture

The application must separate data sources from the UI.

    Data Provider
         │
         ├── DummyDataProvider
         │
         ├── WeatherAPIProvider
         │
         └── SensorDataProvider
                Future
         │
         ↓
    Environment Engine
         ↓
    Application

Initially:

    Dummy Data
         ↓
    Application

Later:

    Physical Sensors
         ↓
    Sensor Provider
         ↓
    Same Application

The frontend should not require a major rewrite when sensors are added.

---

## 14. Sensor Integration — Future

Physical sensors must NOT be part of the first MVP.

Later architecture:

    ESP32
      ↓
    CO₂ Sensor
    Temperature Sensor
    Humidity Sensor
      ↓
    MQTT / HTTP
      ↓
    Backend
      ↓
    SensorDataProvider
      ↓
    Existing Application

The goal is to make sensor integration an additional data source rather than a complete application redesign.

---

## 15. Scientific Principle

The application must not use the simplified assumption:

    More people = oxygen deficiency

Instead, model:

    Occupancy
        +
    Ventilation
        +
    Room Characteristics
        ↓
    Indoor Environmental Conditions

CO₂ and ventilation should be major variables in the simulation.

O₂ should be treated as a measured/simulated environmental parameter.

---

## 16. Medical Visualization

If human-body visualization is included, it should be educational only.

Possible visual indicators:

- Eye irritation
- Fatigue
- Headache
- Respiratory discomfort

The application must clearly state:

> This visualization represents possible environmental effects and is not a medical diagnosis.

---

## 17. Development Priority

### Phase 1

Build the complete application with dummy data.

### Phase 2

Add real-time simulation.

### Phase 3

Add Chennai weather API.

### Phase 4

Add outdoor AQI integration.

### Phase 5

Add advanced 3D visualization.

### Phase 6

Add physical sensors.

---

## 18. MVP Definition

The MVP is complete when:

- [ ] IT office renders correctly
- [ ] People can be added/removed
- [ ] Room size is adjustable
- [ ] Ventilation is adjustable
- [ ] AC is adjustable
- [ ] Dummy data updates in real time
- [ ] CO₂ changes according to simulation
- [ ] Temperature changes according to simulation
- [ ] Humidity changes according to simulation
- [ ] O₂ is displayed
- [ ] Airflow animation works
- [ ] Green/Yellow/Red status works
- [ ] Dashboard works
- [ ] Live charts work
- [ ] Scenario mode works
- [ ] Chennai weather API works
- [ ] Outdoor and indoor data are clearly separated
- [ ] No physical sensor is required
- [ ] Future sensor integration is supported by the architecture

---

## 19. Final Product Goal

The final application should feel like a **living interactive office environment**.

Users should be able to change:

    People
    Room
    Ventilation
    AC
    Doors / Windows

and immediately see:

    CO₂
    O₂
    Temperature
    Humidity
    Airflow
    Environmental Status
    Charts
    Alerts
    Recommendations

change in real time.

---

## 20. Final Goal Statement

> **AirSense aims to create a real-time interactive 3D IT office environment that combines Chennai outdoor weather and air-quality context with adjustable indoor occupancy and ventilation parameters to visualize changing indoor environmental conditions. The first version will use reliable simulated data and real-time APIs, while the architecture will remain ready for physical sensor integration in the future.**

---

## 21. Core Development Principle

**Do not start with hardware.**

Build:

    Dummy Data
        ↓
    Real-Time Simulation
        ↓
    Interactive Office
        ↓
    Dashboard
        ↓
    Chennai Weather API
        ↓
    Outdoor AQI
        ↓
    Working MVP
        ↓
    Physical Sensors Later

The priority is:

**Working software first → real hardware later.**
